From 5b558ee6b05de75dde25f163fa6feefa1f5599c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:32:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ui: retire the Network Map - the dashboard takes its rail
 slot and its header button goes

Owner item. Three parts, one shape: the stock Network Map (index.asp,
NETWORKMAP_PAGE in shared.h) is superseded by the Reaper dashboard, so it should
not be reachable and should not occupy the first slot in the nav.

1. DISCONNECTED. reaper_inject.c's injected bounce redirected index.asp to the
dashboard only when it loaded as the TOP document. Framed, it still rendered -
which is exactly what the rail did with it. It now redirects the TOP window in
BOTH contexts, so a bookmark, a stock in-page link or a stray frame target all
land on the dashboard. It gets its own line rather than a SUP{} entry because
SUP targets are FRAMED pages ("/reaper_shell.asp#" + target) and the dashboard is
top-level.

Verified by extracting the REAPER_BOUNCE_JS macro exactly as the preprocessor
concatenates it and running it against a stubbed location/self/top:

  index.asp        top-level -> /Main_ReaperDash.asp     (unchanged)
  index.asp        FRAMED    -> /Main_ReaperDash.asp     (NEW - used to stay put)
  QoS_EZQoS (SUP)  both      -> /reaper_shell.asp#Reaper_QoS.asp   (unchanged)
  Advanced_LAN     top-level -> /reaper_shell.asp#...    (unchanged)
  Advanced_LAN     FRAMED    -> stays put                (unchanged)

2. RAIL. The Network Map entry in menuTrees/menuTree.js (and the railFallback
copy in reaper_shell.asp, and the hardcoded rail in Main_ReaperDash.asp - all
three must move together, standing rule 6/20) now points at the dashboard. The
dashboard carries its OWN chrome, so framing it would paint the header and rail
twice: buildRail() gained isTopLevelPage(), which emits it as a plain navigation
link with no data-page, so the framing click handler leaves it alone. Verified by
running the shipped buildRail() against a stub menuTree - dashboard renders as
href="/Main_ReaperDash.asp" with no data-page, stock entries still frame, an
addon's off-origin entry still opens in a new tab, and no index.asp remains.

3. HEADER. The Dashboard button is removed. With the dashboard owning the first
rail slot, a second entry point beside Reboot/Logout was redundant; the brand
logo still links there as it always has.

NEW TOKEN Reaper_c_dashboard, translated into all 25 packs rather than reusing
ASUS's AiProtection_title_Dashboard_title - whose FR value is "Page de jeu"
(game page), which is right for the ROG dashboard it was written for and wrong
for a primary nav label. Wording matches the "dashboard" phrasing already used
inside RFWU_15 per language. Dicts stay in lockstep at 6297 lines, identical key
order; all 475 page/language combinations still compile.

NOT BUILT. Metal: confirm the rail's first item goes to the dashboard without
framing it, that the header no longer shows the button, and that a manual
/index.asp lands on the dashboard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
